   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<p>Hello admin,</p>\n\n<p>I am attempting to create a PCA plot using a SNP dataset\nobtained from the Dartseq method. I have filtered the SNPs using the dart\npackage function. However, when I attempt to generate the PCA plot using the\nfollowing command, an error occurs. Could you please assist me in identifying\nwhat is wrong with the command line? It appears that there may be an issue with\nthe genlight data (f4).</p>\n\n<p>Thank you.<br><br><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">library(dartR)\n</span></span><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">library(directlabels)\n</span></span><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">library(plotly)\n</span></span><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">pcoa &lt;- gl.pcoa(f4)\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,154,6)\">Starting gl.pcoa </span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,154,6)\">  Processing genlight object with SNP data</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,154,6)\">  Performing a PCA, individuals as entities, loci as attributes, SNP genotype as state</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,154,6)\">Completed: gl.pcoa </span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">\n</span></span><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">gl.pcoa.plot(glPca = pcoa,\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             x= f4,\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             interactive = TRUE)\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,154,6)\">Starting gl.pcoa.plot </span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,154,6)\">  Processing an ordination file (glPca)</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,154,6)\">  Processing genlight object with SNP data</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in data.frame(..., check.names = FALSE) : \n  arguments imply differing number of rows: 45, 0</span></span></span><br></p>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "tFpmaXSGAAAJ",
   "from": "Jose Luis Mijangos",
   "author": "592079bda2cb3220",
   "date": "2024-02-15T05:51:08Z",
   "subject": "Re: Issue with gl.pcoa()",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi,<div><br></div><div>I guess that the problem is that your individuals in your genlight object do not have a population assigned.</div><div>As mentioned in the information provided in the heading of this forum, you can use the function  gl.compliance.check() as shown below:</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>library(dartR)<br>t1 &lt;- <a href=\"http://platypus.gl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://platypus.gl&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792458038050000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3bia9kz9NqD6mgcdd7s1KJ\">platypus.gl</a><br>t1$pop &lt;- NULL<br>t1 &lt;- gl.compliance.check(t1)<br>pcoa &lt;- gl.pcoa(t1)<br>gl.pcoa.plot(pcoa,t1)<br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div>Luis </div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><br></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thursday 15 February 2024 at 4:39:37 pm UTC+11 <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">afiam...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><p>Hello admin,</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I am attempting to create a PCA plot using a SNP dataset\r\nobtained from the Dartseq method. I have filtered the SNPs using the dart\r\npackage function. However, when I attempt to generate the PCA plot using the\r\nfollowing command, an error occurs. Could you please assist me in identifying\r\nwhat is wrong with the command line? It appears that there may be an issue with\r\nthe genlight data (f4).</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Thank you.<br><br><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">library(dartR)\r\n</span></span><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">library(directlabels)\r\n</span></span><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">library(plotly)\r\n</span></span><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">pcoa &lt;- gl.pcoa(f4)\r\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,154,6)\">Starting gl.pcoa </span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">\r\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,154,6)\">  Processing genlight object with SNP data</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">\r\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,154,6)\">  Performing a PCA, individuals as entities, loci as attributes, SNP genotype as state</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">\r\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,154,6)\">Completed: gl.pcoa </span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">\r\n</span></span><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:blue\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">gl.pcoa.plot(glPca = pcoa,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             x= f4,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">             interactive = TRUE)\r\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,154,6)\">Starting gl.pcoa.plot </span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">\r\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,154,6)\">  Processing an ordination file (glPca)</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">\r\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;color:rgb(78,154,6)\">  Processing genlight object with SNP data</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px\">\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in data.frame(..., check.names = FALSE) : \r\n  arguments imply differing number of rows: 45, 0</span></span></span><br></p></blockquote></div>"
